      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`/v1/responses` accepts a LoRA adapter in the `model` parameter (for example `model=\"base:adapter1\"`), and `_validate_model` even documents that adapters may be addressed by name or through the `base:adapter` form. However, the request is forwarded to the engine without `lora_path`, so the base model serves the request and the client gets a normal HTTP 200 response. The adapter is silently ignored.\n\nChat and Completions already resolve the adapter with `_resolve_lora_path` and pass it to `GenerateReqInput`. Responses does not.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`create_responses` validates `request.model` but never resolves or forwards `lora_path`:\n\n`python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/serving_responses.py:349`\n\n```python\nmodel_error = self._validate_model(request.model)\nif model_error is not None:\n    return model_error\n```\n\nThe initial `GenerateReqInput` is built without `lora_path`, and the request rebuilt after a built-in tool call also omits it.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Resolve the adapter once in `create_responses` with the same `_resolve_lora_path(request.model, None)` helper used by Chat/Completions.\n- Pass `lora_path` to the initial `GenerateReqInput`.\n- Preserve `adapted_request.lora_path` when rebuilding the request after a built-in tool call.\n- Add regression tests for the initial request and the tool-call continuation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/entrypoints/openai/test_serving_responses.py -k \"lora_adapter or standalone_builtin_tools\" -q` -> 2 passed.\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/entrypoints/openai/test_serving_responses.py::EnginePassthroughTestCase -q` -> 6 passed.\n- The new LoRA test fails on the old code with `AssertionError: None != 'adapter1'`.\n- `pre-commit` passes.\n- The full responses unit file also has 8 unrelated Inkling failures locally because the optional `tml-renderers` package is not installed.\n\n## Accuracy tests\n\nNot applicable: request plumbing only; no model forward or kernel change.\n\n## Speed tests and profiling\n\nNot applicable: one adapter lookup per request; no change to the generation path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit\n- [x] Add and run unit tests\n- [x] Documentation changes not needed\n- [x] Accuracy and speed benchmarks not applicable\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41256266433](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41256266433)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41256266347](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41256266347)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41256266341](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41256266341)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
