  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "This handles `base:adapter`, but `model=\"adapter1\"` still gets served by the base model. `_validate_model` accepts the bare adapter name (and `/v1/models` lists adapters that way), but `_parse_model_parameter` returns no adapter when there's no colon, so `lora_path` ends up None. Could you also set `lora_path = request.model` when it's a registered adapter name and add a test for that form?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:34:56Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -349,6 +349,10 @@ async def create_responses(\n         if model_error is not None:\n             return model_error\n \n+        lora_path = (\n+            self._resolve_lora_path(request.model, None) if request.model else None",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/47661#discussion_r4433037165",
      "id": 4433037165,
      "line": 353,
      "original_line": 353,
      "path": "python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/serving_responses.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T19:34:56Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "paolo-perrone"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Addressed now in c29cfcdf9. \r\n`create_responses` now falls back to `request.model` when it is a registered LoRA adapter name, so both `model=\"base:adapter1\"` and `model=\"adapter1\"` set `lora_path`. \r\nAlso added a regression test for the bare-name form.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-01T00:23:56Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -349,6 +349,10 @@ async def create_responses(\n         if model_error is not None:\n             return model_error\n \n+        lora_path = (\n+            self._resolve_lora_path(request.model, None) if request.model else None",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/47661#discussion_r4433819666",
      "id": 4433819666,
